# ForkSC Open Licence V1.0

**Effective: March 2026**

---

## 1. Definitions

**"The Specification"** means the ForkSC architecture specification, junction tag schema, and all associated documentation published in this repository.

**"State Cache Systems"** means the entity designated as the IP steward of the ForkSC specification and the enforcer of the Civic Covenant.

**"Commercial Use"** means any use of an implementation of the Specification in a product, service, or system that generates revenue, or is deployed within an organisation that generates revenue, whether or not the implementation itself is the revenue source.

**"Non-Commercial Use"** means use for personal learning, academic research, non-profit civic administration, and any use by a Qualifying Civic Entity as defined below.

**"Qualifying Civic Entity"** means any of the following: a Community Land Trust registered under applicable legislation; a Community Benefit Society with a statutory asset lock; a Ward-level or equivalent local governance body operating under a sovereign commons framework; a non-profit municipal organisation whose primary purpose is community governance; and any community governance framework that preserves the invariant core commitments of The Sovereign Commons (community land sovereignty, mutual credit as commons infrastructure, AI-assisted administration with legible reasoning, restorative conflict resolution, and civic education as ongoing governance capacity).

---

## 2. Non-Commercial and Civic Use

The Specification is freely available for Non-Commercial Use. No licence fee, no registration, no conditions beyond preservation of this licence notice in derivative works.

Qualifying Civic Entities may use, implement, deploy, modify, and distribute implementations of the Specification — including locally hosted, air-gapped deployment — at zero cost, in perpetuity, without condition.

---

## 3. Commercial Use

Commercial Use of any implementation of the Specification requires a commercial licence from State Cache Systems.

Commercial licence terms will be published separately and will be structured to be accessible to small and medium-sized enterprises, not only to well-resourced corporations.

Every commercial licence issued carries the Civic Covenant (Section 4) as a non-waivable, non-severable condition.

---

## 4. The Civic Covenant

The Civic Covenant is a founding structural condition of this licence. It is not a charitable concession. It is an architectural feature of the ForkSC specification.

**4.1** Every commercial implementation of the Specification must provide perpetual, zero-cost, full-stack access to Qualifying Civic Entities. This includes the right to locally host, air-gap, and operate the implementation without any dependency on the commercial provider's infrastructure, pricing, or continued existence.

**4.2** The Civic Covenant is irrevocable. It survives any change of ownership, acquisition, merger, restructuring, bankruptcy, or dissolution of any commercial entity holding a licence under this agreement.

**4.3** The Civic Covenant is non-waivable. No Qualifying Civic Entity may be asked or required to waive their rights under the Covenant as a condition of any agreement.

**4.4** Violation of the Civic Covenant constitutes automatic termination of the commercial licence.

---

